A||N||6||pherder||Phantom wiper swipe.||||1||
Z||000000||pherder||07-27-2001||04:03 PM||||In a past thread, I made the statement that in every case of several Fieros that I owned that had the phantom wiper swipe, when I replaced the switch in the steering column, it fixed it.  Period.  <P>Until this last one.  Replaced the switch.  Phantom wiper swipe when I turned the ignition switch to start and let go to the run position.  It then started to get worst.  Whenever I touched the turn signal stalk, even to just set the cruise control, I would get the wiper swipe.  I disconnected the switch completely and then all I would get was the phantom wiper swipe on start up.  That made me think that something other than the switch was the problem.<P>Someone else stated that it was the central ground (G201) under the dash that was the problem.  I took off the dash to find that !@#$!#@ connection (now I know where it is and can get to it without taking the dash off!)  Unfortunately, that wasn't the problem unless the ground wire connection <B>INSIDE</B> the wiring harness had come apart or corroded.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I then remembered someone saying that it was the wiper motor circuit board.  I took mine off and started to replace it with the one from my Formula.<P>Here is why I didn't.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wb_88_front.jpg">   <P>Notice the upper left hand corner of the circuit board.  The diode is blown apart and half of it is missing!<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wp_88_rear.jpg">    <P>This is the rear of the same circuit board.  Notice the discoloration?<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wp_86_rear.jpg">    <P>This is the board that was in my 86 SE that was giving me the phantom wiper swipe.  The component side looks good.  The rear has the same discoloration.  I plan on trying to take the good diode off the one board and putting it in the other board and see if I can make one good board out of two.<P>I got a replacement board out of an Astro Van (of all things!).  Seems they (and their cousins) use the same wiper motor/circuit board arrangement as the 85-88 Fiero.  The one 84 Fiero that was at the salvage yard I was at, had a different wiper motor.<P>BTW, I found the EGR cover that is being sold on eBay by several different people on a mid-size GM cars with 3100/3300 engines.  I just did a quick look and found two ... one was cracked and the other is now on my 86 SE!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  $5 got the circuit board and the EGR cover!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-27-2001||07:03 PM||||That is what my board looked like and my diodes were shot as well.  I replaced the board with one I bought from the dealer and the wipers worked but I kept getting the phantom wipe.  Turns out that the wiper motor itself was bad as well.  I opened the motor and tried to mess with the cam contacts but that did not help.  I finally broke down and bought a wiper motor.  Now my wipers work fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieronv||07-28-2001||04:21 PM||||Where is the wiper control board located? I looked under the dash but I couldn't find it. I'm also having problems with my wiper delay any suggestions.||||reg||5
Z||000003||sparks||07-28-2001||04:28 PM||||I'm having problems with my wipers as well.  I replaced the switch, which fixed the "phantom wipe" problem but I still don't have any speed but high and the washer doesnt' work but on high.<P>I just took my circuit board out too and looked the diode on mine labled D14 which I don't see in the above pictures, same size as D13 and would be to D13's right is discolored on the backside of the board.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>To find your circuit board it's under the hood, not the dash first.<P>Take the cover off that goes along the top of the cowl and holds your air deflector (if you have a sunroof), it's held on with 3 7mm bolts.  Then the motor is exposed, there's a hex head screw in the center of the motor cover, take it off and you'll see the backside of your circuit board.  Gently pull from the passenger side to the front of the car to unplug it and its out.  It's only about 2"X4".<P>Hope that helps!<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||07-28-2001||04:41 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sparks:<BR><B>I just took my circuit board out too and looked the diode on mine labled D14 which I don't see in the above pictures, same size as D13 and would be to D13's right is discolored on the backside of the board.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here is the front side of the 86 board (like yours ... the other one is a newer 88 board)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wp_86_front.jpg">  <P>The large diode (D14) in the center next to the relay is the one that has the circuit board discolored and I believe it is bad but not as bad as the blown up one on the 88 board!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>And as Sparks wrote, this board in under a cover on the front of the wiper motor in the front compartment.  The cover is held on by a single 1/4" screw and the board is just pushed on to 5 connectors so it pulls out pretty easily.<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 07-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||07-28-2001||04:41 PM||||I don't have any problems w/ my wipers. Just wanted to say this kind of post and replys, with pics and expanations are fine bits of 'detective' work and really help us novices. These are the posts that we look for in searches and give us a lot of insight into where to start troubleshoting. Thanks<BR>for the extra effort.<BR>Don ||||reg||1
Z||000006||pherder||07-28-2001||05:12 PM||||Well, I took off the good diode (D13) off the 86 board and replaced the blown up one on the 88 board with it and then plugged it into my 86 SE's wiper motor.  <P>Houston ... we have wiper function!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>So, for $5 at the salvage yard, I got one good working board (and an EGR valve cover  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) and then took the two boards I had (both being bad) and made one good one out of them.<P>I guess I could find replacement diodes and fix the one remaining board but I only have two Fieros (at this time) and now both have good boards so I guess I will just "file" it away for now.<P>Paul||||reg||10
